{"ts": "2026-08-26T11:44:52.355797+00:00", "event": "run_start", "task": "Whence in 12 lines (read SPEC.md with read_file for the full language):\n  let x = 1 + 2                # bind once; same-block rebinding is a parse error\n  fn f(a, b) { a * b }         # last expression is the value; tail calls loop\n  if c { 1 } else { 2 }        # if is an expression; non-bool condition -> miss\n  check \"label\": expr          # test statement, records ok/fail\n  print(x)  print(why x)       # why x = the provenance (why-tree) of x\n  miss \"reason\"                # every runtime error is a propagating `miss`\n  (expr rescue fallback)       # recover from a miss\n  [1, 2] @{k: 1}  xs[0] r.k    # lists, records, index, field\n  snip x  note(\"lbl\", x)       # cut / annotate provenance\n  builtins: len range map filter fold push str num abs sqrt missed reasons\n            contains join keys merge steps at blame diverge contrast\nValues ARE provenance nodes: `why`, `steps(x)`, `at(x, \"let a\")`,\n`diverge(a, b)`, `contrast(a, b)` inspect history and are part of behaviour.\n\nThe test suite of this Whence checkout fails. Output of `pytest -x -q tests`:\n```\nE               │     └─ 1 ← literal  (line 30)\nE               └─ \"took else-branch\" ← literal  (line 30)\nE         ✓ mutual tail recursion\nE         ✗ merged node names both functions (line 38) — value was false\nE         false ← ==  (line 38)\nE         ├─ \"even\" ← step detail  (line 38)\nE         └─ \"even/odd\" ← literal  (line 38)\nE         where the two sides diverge:\nE         origin 1 of 1 (step):\nE         ▶ \"even\" ← step detail  (line 38) │ ▶ \"even/odd\" ← literal  (line 38)\nE         ✗ and answers to either name (v0.4) (line 39) — value was miss: index 0 out of range (len 0) (line 40)\nE         miss ← and  (line 40)\nE         └─ miss ← ==  (line 40)\nE            ├─ miss ← field .count  (line 40)\nE            │  └─ miss ← index index 0 out of range (len 0)  (line 40)\nE            │     ├─ [] ← steps 0 steps matching call odd  (line 40)\nE            │     │  ├─ false ← let e  (line 36)\nE            │     │  │  └─ false ← call even  (line 36)\nE            │     │  │     └─ false ← if took then-branch  (line 35)\nE            │     │  │        ├─ false ← literal  (line 35)\nE            │     │  │        └─ true ← ==  (line 35)\nE            │     │  │           ├─ 0 ← arg n  (line 34)\nE            │     │  │           │  └─ 0 ← -  (line 34)\nE            │     │  │           │     └─ …\nE            │     │  │           └─ 0 ← literal  (line 35)\nE            │     │  └─ \"call odd\" ← literal  (line 40)\nE            │     └─ 0 ← literal  (line 40)\nE            └─ 100002 ← literal  (line 40)\nE         ✓ non-tail recursion still keeps one node per frame\nE         ✓ and still respects max_depth\nE         checks: 5 passed, 5 failed\nE         \nE       assert 1 == 0\nE        +  where 1 = CompletedProcess(args=['/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3', '/private/var/folders/_6/3xh6ssk928jcqvp...ail recursion still keeps one node per frame\\n✓ and still respects max_depth\\nchecks: 5 passed, 5 failed\\n', stderr='').returncode\n\ntests/test_examples.py:118: AssertionError\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nFAILED tests/test_examples.py::test_tco - AssertionError: sum_to(100000) = 50...\n!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! stopping after 1 failures !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n1 failed, 13 passed in 6.84s\n```\nThe tests are correct. Find the defect in whence/*.py and fix it with the smallest change that restores the intended semantics (edit_file replaces one exact occurrence). Do NOT edit anything under tests/. You have 20 tool steps in total; pytest on the whole suite takes 1-3 minutes, so run it at most three times.\noutline/read_file/search share a hard budget of 30 calls; after that they refuse.\nReading code: outline a file, then read_file with start/end (200-line windows); search takes a